# Take-it / Open bid — dedicated agent

This feature has its own branch: `feat/take-it-open-bid`.

**Do not work on:** admin personas, view-as, test-lab, `scripts/setup-admins.ts`, or unrelated Insights/facility work.

## Product names

- **Take-it** (`LoadRateMode.TAKE_IT`) — posted pay rate. Carriers book that number only.
- **Allow counters** — Take-it only. Carriers may still book Take-it instantly, or submit a counter the mill accepts/declines.
- **Open bid** (`LoadRateMode.OPEN_BID`) — no instant book. Carriers bid until the mill accepts or `bidWindowExpiresAt`.

## Behavior

- Book API must use the posted Take-it rate (ignore client-typed rates). Reject Open bid books; tell them to bid.
- One pending bid/counter per carrier per load (update in place).
- Accepting a bid books the load at that amount and declines other pending bids.
- Facility/driver pages must never show rates.

## Key files

- Schema: `Load.rateMode`, `allowCounterOffers`, `bidWindowExpiresAt`, model `LoadBid`
- Labels: `src/lib/rate-mode.ts`
- Accept/expire: `src/lib/load-bids.ts`
- Post UI: `src/components/supplier-post-load-form.tsx`
- Carrier actions: `src/components/carrier-rate-actions.tsx`
- Open Bids page: `src/app/bids/page.tsx` (nav id `openBids`)
- APIs: `POST /api/loads/[loadId]/book`, `POST /api/loads/[loadId]/bids`, `POST /api/bids/[bidId]`, `GET /api/bids`

Wait for the user's feedback before expanding scope (link expiry, site accounts, email, etc.).
